    "en": "Equivalence classes"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "For an equivalence relation, the equivalence class $[a]$ is the set of all elements related to $a$. Two classes are either equal or disjoint, and together they cover the whole set: they form a partition.",
    "kn": "a ಗೆ ಸಂಬಂಧಿಸಿದ ಎಲ್ಲ ಅಂಶಗಳ ಗಣವೇ ಸಮಾನತಾ ವರ್ಗ [a]. ಎರಡು ವರ್ಗಗಳು ಒಂದೇ ಅಥವಾ ಪರಸ್ಪರ ಬೇರ್ಪಟ್ಟಿರುತ್ತವೆ, ಮತ್ತು ಒಟ್ಟಿಗೆ ಇಡೀ ಗಣವನ್ನು ಆವರಿಸುತ್ತವೆ."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "[a] = {x ∈ A : x R a}"
    },
    {
     "en": "Classes are pairwise disjoint"
    },
    {
     "en": "Their union is A"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "The equivalence class of a is everything related to a. Different classes never overlap, and together they fill the whole set.",
